%% MediTrack Part 1 electrical architecture
flowchart LR
  PS1[Certified isolated 5 V USB supply] --> F1[500 mA resettable fuse]
  F1 --> D1[Reverse-polarity protection]
  D1 --> V5[Protected 5 V rail]
  V5 --> U1[ESP32-WROOM-32E dev board]
  V5 --> B1[Active buzzer supply]
  V5 --> F2[Three-servo branch fuse]
  F2 --> SERVO1[5 V servo 1\ncylinder 1 gate]
  F2 --> SERVO2[5 V servo 2\ncylinder 2 gate]
  F2 --> SERVO3[5 V servo 3\ncylinder 3 gate]
  U1 --> V33[3.3 V rail / board regulator]
  V33 --> OLED[SH1106 OLED\nI2C GPIO21/22]
  V33 --> BTN[Three NO buttons\nGPIO4/16/17 to GND]
  LID[Lid microswitch / Hall / reed\nGPIO18, 3.3 V safe] --> U1
  U1 -->|GPIO19| Q1[N-MOSFET low-side driver\n100 kΩ gate pulldown]
  Q1 --> B1
  U1 -->|GPIO23 PWM| SERVO1
  U1 -->|GPIO25 PWM| SERVO2
  U1 -->|GPIO26 PWM| SERVO3
  CHUTE[Optional chute sensor\nGPIO27] --> U1
  U1 -->|GPIO2 + 680 Ω| GREEN[Green LED]
  U1 -->|GPIO15 + 680 Ω| RED[Red LED]
  SW[Optional lid microswitch\nNO contact to GND] -->|alternate J2 sense| U1
  GND[Common GND star/return] --- U1
  GND --- OLED
  GND --- BTN
  GND --- Q1
  GND --- SW
